Summary
In this chapter, we discussed many of the fundamentals of Python extension,
as handled in the python module. However, we did not discuss issues related
to multithreading, while running the Python interpreter. A mutual exclusion
lock (mutex) is necessary, so that the CPython library obtains the “global
interpreter lock” (GIL), when working with shared PyObject s. This ensures
that PyObject s are not updated by more than one running interpreter. The
GIL is managed by various functions of the CPython API.
